 <notes>0.4.14 fixes three byte-path bugs and documents the whole surface. Byte-level Tensor round trips are exact: fromBuffer/toBuffer copy bytes verbatim when the dtype is unchanged and no scale/mean/std is requested, so int64 values above 2^53, INT64_MIN and INT64_MAX survive a round trip instead of being routed through double. Clamping to the int64 upper bound is no longer undefined behaviour (2^63 is not representable as a double; NaN now clamps to INT64_MIN and values at or above 2^63 saturate to INT64_MAX). mean/std now follow the channel axis of the target shape instead of a fixed offset from the end: dim 0 for rank 3, dim 1 for rank >= 4 with the stride taken after C, which also fixes per-channel normalisation for 5D NCDHW. fromBuffer and toBuffer share one option parser. Adds six PHPT cases (039-044) covering the byte API, int64 exactness, rank-3 and rank-5 channel axes, and fixes the two user-reported bugs above. Documentation: EP-CPU, EP-COREML, EP-OPENVINO, EP-CUDA, and an end-to-end YOLO11 + PP-OCR example (examples/openvino-yolo-ocr) with a static-QDQ int8 quantizer and CPU-vs-OpenVINO measurements. package.xml now ships docs, examples and all 44 tests; CI verifies that package.xml and the tree agree. Everything else is preserved.</notes>
